{"title":"Career Roadmap — Microbiologist","role":"Microbiologist","summary":"A Microbiologist studies microorganisms such as bacteria, fungi, viruses, protozoa, and other microscopic biological systems. Microbiologists work across pharmaceuticals, healthcare, food, biotechnology, environmental science, agriculture, research, and industrial microbiology.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Microbiology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Microbiologist studies microorganisms such as bacteria, fungi, viruses, protozoa, and other microscopic biological systems. Microbiologists work across pharmaceuticals, healthcare, food, biotechnology, environmental science, agriculture, research, and industrial microbiology."},{"type":"p","text":"A B.Sc Microbiology graduate can enter laboratory-support, QC, testing, and junior microbiology roles. For advanced research, specialized microbiology, university/research careers, and many higher-level technical positions, an M.Sc Microbiology or related postgraduate qualification is strongly recommended."},{"type":"p","text":"Core career combination:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Microbiology","Laboratory Skills","Molecular Biology","Quality Systems","Data Analysis","Bioinformatics"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Development Focus","Typical Position"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Microbiology fundamentals, laboratory techniques, research exposure"},{"text":"Microbiology Intern / Lab Trainee"}],[{"text":"2030–2033"},{"text":"Culture, identification, testing and documentation"},{"text":"Junior Microbiologist / QC Microbiologist"}],[{"text":"2033–2037"},{"text":"Independent laboratory analysis and specialized testing"},{"text":"Microbiologist"}],[{"text":"2037–2041"},{"text":"Advanced testing, investigations and quality s